NV_PK(25,{"in central and northern taiwan you often see tube mi gao braised pork and mushroom go into the bottom of a small tube sticky rice is packed on top and the tubes are steamed it is turned out onto a plate like a little hill and covered with sweet chili sauce the tubes used to be made of bamboo which is how it got its name":"","in tainan people often have mi gao with a bowl of four herb soup or fish ball soup":"","one mi gao and one four herb soup please":"","fatty pork or lean pork":"","no sweet chili sauce please":"","tainan sticky rice mi gao":"","catch the ingredients for tainan sticky rice mi gao":"","2 cups of sticky rice":"","200 g braised minced pork":"","4 tbsp fish floss":"","4 tbsp braised peanuts":"","soak the sticky rice for three hours and drain it":"","steam the rice for thirty minutes until the grains are soft and springy":"","slice the cucumber thinly and mix it with a little salt":"","put the rice in a small bowl and pour a spoonful of minced pork on top":"","add the fish floss cucumber and peanuts":"","sprinkle a little water on the rice halfway through steaming and it will not dry out":"","tainan mi gao is a small bowl of steamed sticky rice topped with minced pork fish floss cucumber and peanuts":"","tainan mi gao is white sticky rice with minced pork on top":"","tube mi gao is steamed in a small tube and turned out onto a plate":""});